       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks like an error.\n\nMetformin 2550 mg three times daily comes to 7,650 mg/day. That is 3 times the FDA maximum of 2,550 mg/day. A single 2,550 mg dose already equals the maximum for a whole day. At this dose the risk of lactic acidosis is high, even with normal renal function.\n\nYou may have meant one of these:\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals** (2,550 mg/day total), which is the usual maximum.\n- A lower dose, such as 500 mg or 1,000 mg twice daily, or another regimen.\n\nTell me which dose and frequency you want and I'll enter it right away. If 2,550 mg per dose three times daily is what you intend, tell me that and I'll enter it with a note recording that you confirmed it."
