       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order as written, even with your confirmation. 7,650 mg/day of metformin is three times the maximum labeled dose. I know of no indication that would justify it. It carries a serious risk of lactic acidosis, and a 70 kg patient with normal renal function isn't protected from that.\n\nI can enter any of these right away:\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals** (2,550 mg/day, the usual maximum)\n- A lower or titrated regimen, such as 500 mg twice daily, increased as tolerated\n- An extended-release formulation, up to 2,000 mg once daily with the evening meal\n\nIf you have a specific reason for the higher dose, such as a protocol or a transcription issue, please talk to the pharmacy or clinical decision support team first. The order can go in once it has been through that review."
